World "Sentences"
Title "From connectives to sentences"

Introduction "
Peters (1979) gave Karttunen's filtering conditions a truth-conditional form with the Middle
Kleene connectives of the last world. In this world the connectives meet sentences, and a theory
of projection becomes a claim about which contexts accept which sentences.

The example is the one from the last world: *France has a king and the king of France is bald*,
and the same conjunction in the other order.
"
